<title>USA: Owens sees 1998 passing $5 bln sales target.</title>
<headline>Owens sees 1998 passing $5 bln sales target.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens Corning said Thursday it expected to surpass in 1998 the $5 billion sales target that it had set for itself for the year 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;With the help of recent strategic acquisitions that enhance our System Thinking offering, in 1998 we will exceed the $5 billion sales target that we originally established for the year 2000,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company reported a profit of $1.11 per diluted share for the second quarter, compared with $1.25 excluding special charges for the same period last year.</p>
</text>
